{#-
  Technology explainer page — ENGLISH ONLY (singleLocale). Deliberately
  short and visual: the core technology story only. Longer Q&A and the
  glossary live on /technology/faq.html (linked from the footer and the
  bottom of this page). Citations render from src/_data/technologyPage.js
  so the visible reference list and the TechArticle `citation` schema
  share one source.

  Wording rules (approved): no "zero spread / perfect / zero noise /
  always better"; Athlos sensors are direct conversion with
  charge-integrating readout — single-photon SENSITIVE, not
  photon-counting. Historical papers are background only, never current
  product specs.
-#}
{%- set tp = technologyPage %}
  <main>

    <!-- HERO -->
    <section class="tech-hero">
      <div class="tech-hero-content">
        <span class="product-category">Technology</span>
        <h1 class="tech-hero-headline">Direct Conversion X-ray Imaging Technology</h1>
        <p class="tech-hero-sub">
          Direct conversion removes the scintillator light-spread stage, creating a shorter and more localized X-ray-to-signal pathway.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CORE VISUAL STORY -->
    <section class="tech-section tech-section--light" id="how-it-works">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="tech-section-head">
          <p class="section-eyebrow reveal">How it works</p>
          <h2 class="section-headline reveal">From X-ray photon to digital signal</h2>
          <p class="tech-lead reveal">
            Conventional detectors take a detour through visible light. Athlos direct conversion sensors don't — they turn X-rays into signal in a single, localized step.
          </p>
        </div>

        {#- shared gradient/filter defs for the three story SVGs -#}
        <svg class="dcs-defs" width="0" height="0" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
          <defs>
            <linearGradient id="ts-slab" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1">
              <stop offset="0" stop-color="#eaf4fb"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="#d3e4ef"/>
            </linearGradient>
            <linearGradient id="ts-cmos" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1">
              <stop offset="0" stop-color="#e9edf1"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="#d6dee4"/>
            </linearGradient>
            <linearGradient id="ts-scint" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1">
              <stop offset="0" stop-color="#fdf3d6"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="#f6e3ab"/>
            </linearGradient>
            <radialGradient id="ts-glow" cx="0.5" cy="0.5" r="0.5">
              <stop offset="0" stop-color="#ffffff" stop-opacity="0.95"/>
              <stop offset="0.4" stop-color="#7dbfe8" stop-opacity="0.7"/>
              <stop offset="1" stop-color="#43a1d8" stop-opacity="0"/>
            </radialGradient>
            <radialGradient id="ts-cloud" cx="0.5" cy="0.5" r="0.5">
              <stop offset="0" stop-color="#fff4cf" stop-opacity="0.95"/>
              <stop offset="0.45" stop-color="#ffd86b" stop-opacity="0.6"/>
              <stop offset="1" stop-color="#f0b429" stop-opacity="0"/>
            </radialGradient>
            <filter id="ts-blur" x="-60%" y="-60%" width="220%" height="220%"><feGaussianBlur stdDeviation="3.4"/></filter>
          </defs>
        </svg>

        <div class="tech-story">
          <!-- STEP 1 · INDIRECT -->
          <article class="tech-story-panel reveal">
            <span class="tech-story-tag tech-story-tag--muted">Conventional</span>
            <div class="tech-story-figure" role="img" aria-label="Indirect conversion: an X-ray photon enters a scintillator and is converted to visible light, which spreads sideways before reaching the photodiode array below, producing a wide signal footprint.">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 220 210" width="100%" aria-hidden="true">
                <line x1="110" y1="10" x2="110" y2="52" stroke="#43a1d8" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-dasharray="6 4" class="ts-anim-beam"/>
                <polygon points="110,58 105,46 115,46" fill="#43a1d8"/>
                <rect x="24" y="58" width="172" height="44" rx="5" fill="url(#ts-scint)" stroke="#e0b64a" stroke-opacity="0.6"/>
                <text x="30" y="74" class="tech-svg-label" fill="#a07c1c">Scintillator</text>
                <ellipse cx="110" cy="86" rx="10" ry="8" fill="url(#ts-cloud)" class="ts-anim-cloud"/>
                <ellipse cx="110" cy="90" rx="34" ry="13" fill="url(#ts-cloud)" class="ts-anim-cloud ts-anim-cloud--2"/>
                <ellipse cx="110" cy="94" rx="60" ry="15" fill="url(#ts-cloud)" class="ts-anim-cloud ts-anim-cloud--3"/>
                <rect x="24" y="112" width="172" height="26" rx="5" fill="#5a6b76" fill-opacity="0.26" stroke="#5a6b76" stroke-opacity="0.5"/>
                <text x="30" y="129" class="tech-svg-label" fill="#5a6b76">Photodiode array</text>
                <path d="M52 152 q58 26 116 0" stroke="#c0392b" stroke-width="2" fill="none"/>
                <text x="110" y="184" text-anchor="middle" class="tech-svg-label" fill="#c0392b">Wide signal footprint</text>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h3 class="tech-story-title">Indirect conversion</h3>
            <p class="tech-story-copy">In indirect conversion, X-rays are first converted into visible light. Before detection, that light can spread laterally inside the scintillator.</p>
          </article>

          <div class="tech-story-arrow" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 40 24" width="40" height="24"><path d="M4 12h30m0 0l-7-6m7 6l-7 6" stroke="#43a1d8" stroke-width="2" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
          </div>

          <!-- STEP 2 · DIRECT -->
          <article class="tech-story-panel tech-story-panel--accent reveal" data-delay="80">
            <span class="tech-story-tag">Direct conversion</span>
            <div class="tech-story-figure" role="img" aria-label="Direct conversion: an X-ray photon enters a CdTe or silicon semiconductor and generates charge at a localized point, which is collected straight down by the nearest pixel electrode, producing a narrow signal footprint.">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 220 210" width="100%" aria-hidden="true">
                <line x1="110" y1="10" x2="110" y2="52" stroke="#43a1d8" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-dasharray="6 4" class="ts-anim-beam"/>
                <polygon points="110,58 105,46 115,46" fill="#43a1d8"/>
                <rect x="24" y="58" width="172" height="44" rx="5" fill="url(#ts-slab)" stroke="#43a1d8" stroke-opacity="0.45"/>
                <text x="30" y="74" class="tech-svg-label" fill="#2b7bab">CdTe or Si semiconductor</text>
                <circle cx="110" cy="82" r="13" fill="url(#ts-glow)" filter="url(#ts-blur)" class="ts-anim-glow"/>
                <rect x="105" y="80" width="10" height="34" rx="3" fill="#43a1d8" fill-opacity="0.8" class="ts-anim-col"/>
                <rect x="24" y="112" width="172" height="26" rx="5" fill="#5a6b76" fill-opacity="0.26" stroke="#5a6b76" stroke-opacity="0.5"/>
                <text x="30" y="129" class="tech-svg-label" fill="#5a6b76">CMOS / ASIC readout</text>
                <path d="M98 152 q12 10 24 0" stroke="#2e8b57" stroke-width="2" fill="none"/>
                <text x="110" y="184" text-anchor="middle" class="tech-svg-label" fill="#2e8b57">Narrow signal footprint</text>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h3 class="tech-story-title">Direct conversion</h3>
            <p class="tech-story-copy">In direct conversion, the X-ray photon generates charge directly inside the detector material, keeping the signal path shorter and more localized.</p>
          </article>

          <div class="tech-story-arrow" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 40 24" width="40" height="24"><path d="M4 12h30m0 0l-7-6m7 6l-7 6" stroke="#43a1d8" stroke-width="2" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
          </div>

          <!-- STEP 3 · ATHLOS -->
          <article class="tech-story-panel reveal" data-delay="160">
            <span class="tech-story-tag tech-story-tag--muted">Athlos design</span>
            <div class="tech-story-figure" role="img" aria-label="Athlos implementation: a semiconductor detector layer is bonded through bump bonds to a CMOS readout chip, producing a clean digital signal output.">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 220 210" width="100%" aria-hidden="true">
                <rect x="30" y="26" width="160" height="34" rx="5" fill="url(#ts-slab)" stroke="#43a1d8" stroke-opacity="0.45"/>
                <text x="110" y="47" text-anchor="middle" class="tech-svg-label" fill="#2b7bab">Detector (CdTe / Si)</text>
                <g fill="#8ea3b0"><circle cx="62" cy="70" r="4"/><circle cx="93" cy="70" r="4"/><circle cx="124" cy="70" r="4"/><circle cx="155" cy="70" r="4"/></g>
                <rect x="30" y="80" width="160" height="34" rx="5" fill="url(#ts-cmos)" stroke="#5a6b76" stroke-opacity="0.4"/>
                <text x="110" y="101" text-anchor="middle" class="tech-svg-label" fill="#5a6b76">CMOS / ASIC readout</text>
                <path d="M110 118 v14 m0 0l-5-6m5 6l5-6" stroke="#43a1d8" stroke-width="1.8" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
                <path class="ts-anim-pulse" d="M40 168 H92 V148 H128 V168 H180" stroke="#43a1d8" stroke-width="2.5" fill="none" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-linecap="round"/>
                <text x="110" y="192" text-anchor="middle" class="tech-svg-label" fill="#2b7bab">Clean digital signal</text>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h3 class="tech-story-title">Athlos implementation</h3>
            <p class="tech-story-copy">Athlos designs direct conversion sensors where the detector material and readout electronics work together as a compact imaging system.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- WHY LOCALIZATION MATTERS -->
    <section class="tech-section tech-section--dark" id="why-localization">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="tech-section-head">
          <p class="section-eyebrow section-eyebrow--light reveal">The advantage</p>
          <h2 class="section-headline section-headline--light reveal">Why localization matters</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="tech-why">
          <div class="tech-why-card reveal">
            <span class="tech-why-num">01</span>
            <h3 class="tech-why-title">Shorter signal path</h3>
            <p class="tech-why-copy">The X-ray becomes signal in one step, inside the detector material — no detour through a light-conversion layer.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="tech-why-card reveal" data-delay="60">
            <span class="tech-why-num">02</span>
            <h3 class="tech-why-title">Reduced light-spread stage</h3>
            <p class="tech-why-copy">Removing the scintillator removes a dominant source of lateral signal spreading found in indirect detectors.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="tech-why-card reveal" data-delay="120">
            <span class="tech-why-num">03</span>
            <h3 class="tech-why-title">More localized footprint</h3>
            <p class="tech-why-copy">Charge is collected close to where the photon was absorbed, helping preserve a compact signal footprint.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="tech-why-card reveal" data-delay="180">
            <span class="tech-why-num">04</span>
            <h3 class="tech-why-title">Built for high-resolution imaging</h3>
            <p class="tech-why-copy">A more localized pathway supports the sharpness and contrast that demanding dental, medical and industrial imaging rely on.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ATHLOS PRODUCT CONNECTION -->
    <section class="tech-section tech-section--light" id="across-sensors">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="tech-section-head">
          <p class="section-eyebrow reveal">In our products</p>
          <h2 class="section-headline reveal">Direct conversion across Athlos sensors</h2>
          <p class="tech-lead reveal">Every Athlos sensor is a direct conversion detector. Two material platforms cover the range from compact intraoral imaging to high-speed industrial scanning.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="tech-products">
          <a class="tech-product-card reveal" href="/products/wios.html">
            <span class="tech-product-kicker">Si-CMOS · intraoral</span>
            <h3 class="tech-product-name">DC-Air®</h3>
            <p class="tech-product-copy">Wireless intraoral dental sensor built on Si-CMOS direct conversion for a compact, high-resolution format.</p>
            <span class="tech-product-link">Explore DC-Air →</span>
          </a>
          <a class="tech-product-card reveal" data-delay="80" href="/products/ufs.html">
            <span class="tech-product-kicker">CdTe-CMOS · line-scan</span>
            <h3 class="tech-product-name">UFS &amp; Industrial IP67 TDI</h3>
            <p class="tech-product-copy">CdTe-CMOS scanning sensors for dental panoramic, medical and inline industrial inspection — TDI scanning at high line rates.</p>
            <span class="tech-product-link">Explore scanning sensors →</span>
          </a>
          <a class="tech-product-card reveal" data-delay="160" href="/products/manufacturing.html">
            <span class="tech-product-kicker">CdTe &amp; Si · platforms</span>
            <h3 class="tech-product-name">Detector platforms &amp; services</h3>
            <p class="tech-product-copy">Contract detector manufacturing and software — the bump-bonding, assembly and signal processing behind direct conversion.</p>
            <span class="tech-product-link">Manufacturing &amp; software →</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- SCIENTIFIC FOUNDATION -->
    <section class="tech-section tech-section--dark tech-section--tight" id="foundation">
      <div class="container container--narrow">
        <div class="tech-section-head">
          <p class="section-eyebrow section-eyebrow--light reveal">Credibility</p>
          <h2 class="section-headline section-headline--light reveal">Built on decades of detector development</h2>
          <p class="tech-lead tech-lead--dark reveal">
            Athlos direct conversion technology builds on more than 30 years of detector development by the same founding team — first at Simage Oy (1993), then Ajat Oy (2001). Their peer-reviewed work laid the groundwork for today's CdTe-CMOS and Si-CMOS sensors. These papers are historical background and evidence of long-term expertise, not descriptions of current product specifications.
          </p>
        </div>
        <ul class="tech-foundation-list reveal">
{%- for c in tp.citations %}
          <li>{% if c.url %}<a href="{{ c.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ c.title }}</a>{% else %}{{ c.title }}{% endif %} <span class="tech-foundation-meta">— {{ c.venue }}, {{ c.year }}</span></li>
{%- endfor %}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- FAQ LINK + CTA -->
    <section class="product-cta" id="contact">
      <div class="container" style="text-align:center;">
        <p class="tech-faq-cta reveal">
          Looking for more technical detail? <a href="/technology/faq.html">Read the Technology FAQ →</a>
        </p>
        <p class="section-eyebrow section-eyebrow--light reveal">Get in Touch</p>
        <h2 class="section-headline section-headline--light reveal" style="max-width:640px;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto;">Discuss direct conversion for your application.</h2>
        <p class="reveal" style="font-size:var(--text-base);font-weight:300;line-height:1.75;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.6);max-width:560px;margin:0 auto 2rem;">
          Whether you are designing a new imaging system or evaluating detector technologies for an existing platform, the Athlos team can support you from specification through integration.
        </p>
        <div class="reveal" style="display:flex;gap:1rem;justify-content:center;flex-wrap:wrap;">
          <a href="/contact.html" class="btn btn-primary">Contact Athlos</a>
          <a href="/products/index.html" class="btn btn-outline">All Products</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>

